# Campaign War Room AI — environment configuration
# Copy this file to backend/.env and fill in the values.
#
# The app technically runs without an API key (using a mock LLM), but every
# article will then be scored as "irrelevant" and the UI will look empty.
# You almost certainly want to configure Groq below.

# ── LLM Provider ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Recommended: groq (free tier, fast, no credit card required).
# Sign up at https://console.groq.com and create an API key.
#
# Options: groq | openai | anthropic | mock
LLM_PROVIDER=groq

# Groq — used when LLM_PROVIDER=groq
# Add extra free-tier keys (each needs its own account at console.groq.com)
GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY_2=
# GROQ_API_KEY_3=
# GROQ_API_KEY_4=
# GROQ_API_KEY_5=
GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# Google Gemini — always used as fallback regardless of LLM_PROVIDER
# Add extra keys for more daily quota (each needs its own Google account at aistudio.google.com)
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY_2=
# GEMINI_API_KEY_3=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# OpenAI — only used if LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Anthropic — only used if LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# ── Search Provider ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Options: mock | tavily
SEARCH_PROVIDER=mock
# Tavily — round-robin across multiple free-tier keys (each account is 1000
# credits/month). Add extras at TAVILY_API_KEY_2, _3, ... — same rotation
# pattern as GROQ_API_KEY_N. Provider quarantines any key returning
# 401/402/429/432 (monthly-quota-exhausted) until process restart.
# TAVILY_API_KEY=
# TAVILY_API_KEY_2=
# TAVILY_API_KEY_3=

# ── Scheduled RSS Ingestion ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
RSS_AUTO_INGEST_ENABLED=true
RSS_AUTO_INGEST_INTERVAL_MINUTES=60

# ── Interactive API docs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Swagger UI (/docs), ReDoc (/redoc), and the OpenAPI schema (/openapi.json)
# are DISABLED by default — they list every endpoint and schema, which is
# recon surface we don't want exposed through the public tunnel. Set to true
# only for local debugging when you want to browse the API interactively.
# EXPOSE_API_DOCS=false

# ── Friend-share access codes ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Turn the app into a private preview before you tunnel it to the internet.
# When ACCESS_CODES is empty (or unset), the app runs without auth and shows
# a "Guest" profile bubble. The moment you add any code here, every /api/*
# request requires a valid X-Access-Code header — friends without a code
# get bounced to the /login page.
#
# Format: semicolon-separated entries, each "code:Display Name" with an
# optional ":admin" suffix that grants admin powers (currently: visibility
# of the per-article relevance bucket badge). Initials and a profile-bubble
# color are auto-derived from the name.
#
# ACCESS_CODES=alice-7m4q:Alice Smith;bob-9k2x:Bob Jones;theo-2x8p:Theo Capeilleres:admin
#
# Tips:
# - Pick codes that are easy to share verbally but not guessable (mix of
#   letters and digits, ~8+ chars). They're shared secrets, not passwords.
# - One code per friend so you can tell who's logged in (their initials show
#   in the top-right bubble) and revoke just that friend later by removing
#   their line.
# - Restart the backend after changing this — codes are read once at startup.

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default (no env var set) uses SQLite at backend/war_room.db. That's the
# right choice during the Postgres migration's Phase 1–3 (see
# POSTGRES_MIGRATION_PLAN.md). Set DATABASE_URL to a Postgres connection
# string when you're ready to test against Postgres, and again at Phase 4
# cutover.
#
# For local Postgres 15 with the `noctua` database created earlier:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://theo@localhost:5432/noctua
#
# For a managed host (Neon/Supabase/RDS), the host gives you a URL like:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://user:pass@host.region.neon.tech/noctua?sslmode=require
